# What never needs to reach the Docker daemon.
#
# Two reasons to keep this tight: a smaller context is a faster build, and
# anything listed here cannot end up in a layer by accident — which is the
# point of the `.env` and `data/` entries below.

# Installed and built inside the image, from the lockfile.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
dist-types
**/dist-types
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. The container gets its configuration from compose, never from a
# file baked into the image.
.env
.env.*

# The runtime data directory is a volume — nothing in it belongs in a layer.
# The seed files the image needs at /app/seed live in `seed/`, which is source
# data and is deliberately not listed here.
data/**
**/data/**
**/.env
**/.env.*
.playwright-mcp
recovered-session-*.md

# Repo furniture with no role in a build.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.auth
docs
playwright-report
test-results
*.log
logs
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The compose file, the nginx config and the systemd unit describe how to run
# the image; they have no business inside it. The entrypoint does.
infra/**
!infra/docker-entrypoint.sh
!infra/xvfb-exec.sh
